# ==============================================================================
# NPM Runtime Configuration (.npmrc)
# ==============================================================================
# Architectural Overview & Deviations from Tool Defaults
# ==============================================================================
# This configuration file deliberately overrides standard npm package manager
# defaults to maintain reproducible dependency resolution across monorepo workspaces.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deviations from npm Tool Defaults:
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Setting: legacy-peer-deps=true
#
# - npm Tool Default (npm v7+): legacy-peer-deps=false
#   By default, npm automatically attempts to install all peer dependencies and halts
#   with a fatal ERESOLVE error whenever conflicting peer dependency versions are encountered.
#
# - Deliberate Deviation: legacy-peer-deps=true (reverting to npm v6 resolution semantics)
#
# - Architectural Rationale & Why Reverting Breaks the Build:
#   In this multi-package monorepo, web3 ecosystem libraries (@stellar/stellar-sdk,
#   Soroban client bindings) and modern frontend tooling (Next.js/React, TypeScript 5,
#   Storybook) specify mutually conflicting peer dependency semver ranges.
#   Without legacy-peer-deps=true, running `npm ci` or `npm install` in CI/CD environments
#   fails immediately with ERESOLVE dependency tree collision errors.
#   Setting legacy-peer-deps=true allows npm to build deterministic dependency trees
#   guided by package-lock.json without requiring manual, fragile dependency overrides.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

legacy-peer-deps=true
